Initial cargo generate-lockfile --offline used absolute cargo path but PATH lacked rustc; it returned: could not execute process rustc -vV (never executed), No such file or directory. No component build ran. Retried with /opt/homebrew/opt/rustup/bin prepended to PATH; lockfile generated successfully.
Initial native verifier stopped before compiling Rust: caller-CIE mutation was rejected by the generic FDE parser as unsupported version 0, before the intended pinned-CIE gate. Moved exact bound-CIE validation ahead of decoding. Repeated the complete verifier in a fresh directory. No Rust source, frozen input, expectation or oracle was changed.
Initial archive-control/manifest command was invoked from packet directory although its Python paths were repository-relative; it failed with FileNotFoundError before changing packet files. Repeated Python generation from repository root, then invoked shasum from packet directory.
